pkg/flag keeps every flag group, so trivy-cdxgen still accepts and ignores
the same flags, environment variables and trivy.yaml keys as before. What
goes is what the flag package imported only for defaults and option helpers
the wrapper never calls:

- rego, policy, result and the DB packages for default values, inlined;
- k8s.io/api for the toleration type of the Kubernetes flags;
- pkg/vex for the type of the VEX sources;
- pkg/result, pkg/rpc/client and pkg/plugin for FilterOpts,
  RemoteCacheOpts, ClientScannerOpts and output plugins.

The runner rejects --server, --output plugin=... and a redis cache backend
before scanning, so none of those paths is reachable.

